#: ../../../how-to/use-uv-backend.rst:3
msgid "Use the uv backend"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/use-uv-backend.rst:5
msgid ""
"Make pipx use `uv <https://github.com/astral-sh/uv>`_ to create virtual "
"environments and install packages in place of `pip <https://pip.pypa.io/>`__ "
"and venv. The CLI surface stays the same."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/use-uv-backend.rst:8
msgid ""
"For why uv is faster and how pipx compares to Astral's standalone ``uv "
"tool``, see :doc:`../explanation/comparisons`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/use-uv-backend.rst:12
msgid "Make uv available"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/use-uv-backend.rst:14
msgid "Install pipx with the ``uv`` extra so it ships the bundled binary:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/use-uv-backend.rst:16
msgid "$ pipx install pipx[uv]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/use-uv-backend.rst:20
msgid ""
"Or install uv 0.9.17 or newer however you like (``brew install uv``, ``cargo "
"install uv``) and put it on ``PATH``; pipx picks it up. New venvs then "
"default to uv. Existing venvs keep their recorded backend. When the uv pipx "
"finds is older than that, pipx warns and falls back to pip. Asking for uv "
"explicitly (``--backend uv``, ``PIPX_DEFAULT_BACKEND=uv``, or a venv that "
"recorded uv) with an older uv fails and asks you to upgrade it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/use-uv-backend.rst:27
msgid "How pipx picks a backend"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/use-uv-backend.rst:49
msgid "Choose a backend explicitly"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/use-uv-backend.rst:51
msgid ""
"$ pipx install black --backend pip\n"
"$ pipx install ruff --backend uv\n"
"$ PIPX_DEFAULT_BACKEND=uv pipx install ruff\n"
"$ pipx environment --value PIPX_RESOLVED_BACKEND"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/use-uv-backend.rst:58
msgid ""
"``install``, ``install-all``, ``inject``, ``upgrade``, ``upgrade-all``, "
"``reinstall``, ``reinstall-all``, and ``run`` all accept ``--backend``. "
"Switch an installed venv with ``pipx reinstall NAME --backend uv``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/use-uv-backend.rst:63
msgid "What changes under uv"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/use-uv-backend.rst:65
msgid ""
"pipx creates venvs with ``uv venv``. The venv contains no ``pip`` and no "
"``pipx_shared.pth`` file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/use-uv-backend.rst:66
msgid ""
"``pipx runpip`` runs ``uv pip <args> --python <venv>/bin/python``. uv "
"rejects flags it does not understand rather than dropping them silently."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/use-uv-backend.rst:68
msgid ""
"``pipx run`` execs ``uv tool run``; its cache lives in uv's cache directory. "
"Pass ``--no-cache`` to skip it or ``--refresh`` to rebuild the cached "
"environment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/use-uv-backend.rst:70
msgid ""
"``pipx run script.py`` execs ``uv run --active --script script.py`` for `PEP "
"723 <https://peps.python.org/pep-0723/>`__ inline scripts, with "
"``VIRTUAL_ENV`` pointing at an environment in pipx's cache."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/use-uv-backend.rst:73
msgid ""
"``--cooldown DAYS`` (or ``PIPX_COOLDOWN``) maps to uv's ``--exclude-newer "
"P{DAYS}D``. See :doc:`Dependency cooldown <dependency-cooldown>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/use-uv-backend.rst:75
msgid ""
"uv reads your user config (``~/.config/uv/uv.toml``, ``%APPDATA%"
"\\uv\\uv.toml`` on Windows), the system config (``/etc/uv/uv.toml``), and a "
"``UV_CONFIG_FILE``, but no project config from your working directory or the "
"script's directory. pipx sets ``UV_PROJECT`` (``--project`` for ``uv run --"
"script``) to ``PIPX_HOME``, replacing any ``UV_PROJECT`` you set, so uv "
"looks for a ``uv.toml`` or a ``pyproject.toml`` with a ``[tool.uv]`` table "
"in ``PIPX_HOME`` and each of its parents up to the filesystem root."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/use-uv-backend.rst:80
msgid ""
"With the default ``PIPX_HOME`` under your home directory, the parents uv "
"searches for project config belong to you or to root. If ``PIPX_HOME`` (or "
"``PIPX_GLOBAL_HOME``) sits below a directory other accounts can write, such "
"as ``/tmp`` or a group-writable share, any of them can place a ``uv.toml`` "
"there that steers pipx's uv calls; keep it in a directory only you can write."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/use-uv-backend.rst:84
msgid ""
"A ``--project``, ``--directory`` or ``--config-file`` in ``--pip-args`` "
"points uv at other configuration, and pipx records it with the environment. "
"On POSIX, a later ``upgrade`` or ``reinstall`` refuses to replay it when "
"another account can change the path. See :doc:`Metadata <../reference/"
"metadata>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/use-uv-backend.rst:90
msgid "Limitations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/use-uv-backend.rst:92
msgid ""
"``pipx install pip --backend uv`` errors: a uv venv has no pip. Use ``--"
"backend pip``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/use-uv-backend.rst:93
msgid ""
"``pipx run --backend uv`` honors ``[pipx.run]`` entry points only where it "
"builds a venv, which with ``--spec`` means an ``<app>`` that differs from "
"the spec's normalized distribution name, or a spec carrying no name at all. "
"An ``<app>`` matching that name goes to ``uv tool run``, which reads console "
"scripts only, so reach for ``--backend pip`` to override a console script of "
"the same name."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/use-uv-backend.rst:97
msgid ""
"Some ``--pip-args`` values have no ``uv tool run`` equivalent (``--"
"editable``, ``--no-build-isolation``); pipx errors instead of dropping them. "
"See :doc:`use-private-index` for which flags uv translates."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/use-uv-backend.rst:99
msgid ""
"``pipx run --backend uv`` rejects ``--system-site-packages``, since uv "
"builds the environment. Use ``--backend pip`` when you need it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/use-uv-backend.rst:101
msgid ""
"``pipx run --backend uv`` against URL or named-pipe scripts falls back to a "
"pipx-managed venv, because ``uv run --script`` reads PEP 723 metadata off "
"disk and runtime-fetched content has no on-disk path. pipx logs a warning."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/use-uv-backend.rst:103
msgid ""
"``pipx run`` falls back to a pipx-managed venv when it has to infer the "
"script name: from a VCS URL, a local project path, or a name it normalizes "
"(``pipx run pip_search`` installs ``pip-search``). ``uv tool run`` takes "
"that name up front and would guess it from the package, so pipx installs the "
"package first and runs the script it declares. Pass ``pipx run --spec <spec> "
"<normalized-name>`` to keep uv's cache when the package declares a matching "
"console script. pipx installs a spec with no distribution name (a path, a "
"URL, a direct reference) twice, once to learn its name and once into the run "
"venv."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/use-uv-backend.rst:112
msgid "Cache layout"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/use-uv-backend.rst:114
msgid ""
"Under the uv backend, ``pipx run APP`` caches in ``UV_CACHE_DIR`` instead of "
"``PIPX_VENV_CACHEDIR``, while ``pipx run script.py`` keeps the script's "
"environment in ``PIPX_VENV_CACHEDIR``. Switching the default backend on a "
"host that already used ``pipx run`` leaves the old pipx cache behind. Find "
"it with ``pipx cache dir`` and remove its environments with ``pipx cache "
"purge``. The 14-day expiry sweep pipx applies to its own cache does not "
"extend to uv's cache, which uv manages on its own schedule (``uv cache "
"clean``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/use-uv-backend.rst:122
msgid "Verify it"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/use-uv-backend.rst:124
msgid "$ pipx environment --value PIPX_RESOLVED_BACKEND"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/use-uv-backend.rst:128
msgid "It prints ``uv`` when pipx will use the uv backend for new venvs."
msgstr ""
